<title>UK: GOLF-LEADING WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Davis Love III has moved</p>
<p>up from 17th to ninth place in the world golf rankings list</p>
<p>after his five-shot victory in the U.S. PGA Championship at</p>
<p>Winged Foot at the weekend.</p>
<p>Top 20 (U.S.) unless stated</p>
<p>  1. Tiger Woods		     10.78 points average</p>
<p>  2. Greg Norman (Australia)     10.22</p>
<p>  3. Ernie Els (South Africa)     9.95</p>
<p>  4. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	  9.64</p>
<p>  5. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)  9.39</p>
<p>  6. Tom Lehman			 8.56</p>
<p>  7. Phil Mickelson		   8.31</p>
<p>  8. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)	  7.98</p>
<p>  9. Davis Love III		   7.61</p>
<p> 10. Mark O'Meara		     7.53</p>
<p> 11. Justin Leonard		   6.90</p>
<p> 12. Fred Couples		     6.67</p>
<p> 13. Nick Faldo (Britain)	   6.57</p>
<p> 14. Scott Hoch			 6.51</p>
<p> 15. Steve Elkington (Australia)  6.48</p>
<p> 16. Brad Faxon			 6.30</p>
<p> 17. Jesper Parnevik (Sweden)     6.18</p>
<p> 18. Vijay Singh (Fiji)	     5.66</p>
<p> 19. Bernhard Langer (Germany)    5.60</p>
<p> 20. Ian Woosnam (Britain)	  5.30</p>
</text>
